<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<usx version="3.0">
  <book code="REV" style="id">REVELATION</book>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="REV 1"/>
  <para style="s1">Prologue and Doxology</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="REV 1:1"/>
    This is the revelation given by Jesus Christ, which God granted to Him so He could show His servants what must happen shortly. Christ communicated this revelation by sending His angel to His servant John,
    <verse eid="REV 1:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="REV 1:2"/>
    who has borne witness to God’s word and to the testimony about Jesus Christ—everything he witnessed.
    <verse eid="REV 1:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="REV 1:3"/>
    Blessed is the person who reads these words, and blessed are those who hear this prophetic message and obey what is written here, for the appointed time is drawing near.
    <verse eid="REV 1:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Greeting and Doxology</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="REV 1:4"/>
    John, writing to the seven congregations throughout the province of Asia:
    <verse eid="REV 1:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">May you experience grace and peace from the One who exists eternally—who is present now, who existed in the past, and who will come in the future; and from the seven Spirits stationed before His throne;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="REV 1:5"/>
    and from Jesus Christ, the trustworthy witness, the firstborn from among the dead, and the supreme ruler over all earthly kings. 
    <verse eid="REV 1:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">To Him who demonstrates His love for us and has liberated us from our sins through the shedding of His blood,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="REV 1:6"/>
    and has constituted us as a kingdom of priests serving His God and Father—to Him belong all glory and dominion throughout eternity. Amen.
    <verse eid="REV 1:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="REV 1:7"/>
    Pay attention. He is coming with the clouds, and every eye will observe Him, including those who pierced Him through with a spear, and all the ethnic groups of the earth will beat their chests in mourning because of Him. This is certain. Amen.
    <verse eid="REV 1:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="REV 1:8"/>
    “I am the Alpha and the Omega—the origin and the goal of all things,” declares the Lord God, “the One who exists eternally—who is present now, who existed in the past, and who will come in the future—the Almighty.”
    <verse eid="REV 1:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Vision of the Son of Man</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="REV 1:9"/>
    I, John, am your brother and companion in the persecution, the kingdom, and the patient endurance that belong to us through our union with Jesus. I found myself on the island named Patmos because I had proclaimed God’s word and maintained my testimony about Jesus.
    <verse eid="REV 1:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="REV 1:10"/>
    I  was in the Spirit on the Lord's day when I heard behind me a thunderous voice like a trumpet blast
    <verse eid="REV 1:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="REV 1:11"/>
    announcing, “Write what you observe in a scroll and dispatch it to the seven churches: to Ephesus, to Smyrna, to Pergamum, to Thyatira, to Sardis, to Philadelphia, and to Laodicea.”
    <verse eid="REV 1:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="REV 1:12"/>
    I turned around to identify the source of the voice addressing me, and when I turned I observed seven lampstands made of gold.
    <verse eid="REV 1:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="REV 1:13"/>
    Moving among the lampstands was someone resembling a human figure, wearing a full-length robe with a golden sash wrapped around His chest.
    <verse eid="REV 1:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="REV 1:14"/>
    His head and hair shone with brilliant whiteness like pure wool or fresh snow, and His eyes blazed like flames of fire.
    <verse eid="REV 1:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="REV 1:15"/>
    His feet gleamed like bronze that has been purified in a smelting furnace, and His voice thundered like the roar of many waters.
    <verse eid="REV 1:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="REV 1:16"/>
    He held seven stars in His right hand, and a sharp sword with two edges emerged from His mouth, and His face radiated brilliance like the sun shining at its peak intensity.
    <verse eid="REV 1:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="REV 1:17"/>
    When I saw Him, I collapsed at His feet as though lifeless. But He placed His right hand on me and said, “Stop being afraid. I am the First and the Last,
    <verse eid="REV 1:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="REV 1:18"/>
    the Living One. I experienced death, but observe—I am alive forevermore, and I possess the keys of death and of Hades. 
    <verse eid="REV 1:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="REV 1:19"/>
    Therefore write down what you have witnessed, both the present realities and the future events that will unfold.
    <verse eid="REV 1:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="REV 1:20"/>
    Concerning the mystery of the seven stars you observed in My right hand and the seven golden lampstands: the seven stars represent the angels or messengers of the seven churches, and the seven lampstands represent the seven churches themselves.
    <verse eid="REV 1:20"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="REV 1"/>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="REV 2"/>
  <para style="s1">To the Church in Ephesus</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="REV 2:1"/>
    “To the angel or messenger of the church in Ephesus, write:
    <verse eid="REV 2:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“These are the declarations of the One who grips the seven stars securely in His right hand and walks among the seven golden lampstands:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="REV 2:2"/>
    ‘I have complete knowledge of your deeds—your exhausting labor and your steadfast endurance. I know you cannot tolerate those who practice evil. You have examined those who falsely claim apostolic authority, and you have exposed them as impostors.
    <verse eid="REV 2:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="REV 2:3"/>
    You have demonstrated perseverance and have endured suffering on account of My name without growing weary.
    <verse eid="REV 2:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="REV 2:4"/>
    ‘Nevertheless, I hold this charge against you: You have abandoned the fervent love you displayed at first.
    <verse eid="REV 2:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="REV 2:5"/>
    Remember the height from which you have fallen. Repent, and resume doing the works you did initially. But if you refuse, I will come to you and remove your lampstand from its position—unless you repent.
    <verse eid="REV 2:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="REV 2:6"/>
    Yet you do possess this commendable quality: You detest the practices of the Nicolaitans, which I also detest.
    <verse eid="REV 2:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="REV 2:7"/>
    ‘Let anyone who has ears pay close attention to what the Spirit is declaring to the churches. To the person who conquers, I will grant authorization to eat from the tree of life standing in God’s paradise.’
    <verse eid="REV 2:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">To the Church in Smyrna</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="REV 2:8"/>
    “To the angel or messenger of the church in Smyrna, write:
    <verse eid="REV 2:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“These are the declarations of the First and the Last, who died and returned to life:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="REV 2:9"/>
    ‘I have full knowledge of your tribulation and your material poverty—though spiritually you are wealthy. I know about the slander hurled at you by those who claim to be Jews but are not genuine Jews; rather, they constitute a synagogue under Satan’s influence.
    <verse eid="REV 2:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="REV 2:10"/>
    Do not fear what you are about to endure. Pay attention. The devil is preparing to cast some of you into prison to test your faithfulness, and you will experience tribulation for ten days. Remain faithful all the way to death, and I will bestow upon you the victor’s crown of life.
    <verse eid="REV 2:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="REV 2:11"/>
    ‘Let anyone who has ears pay close attention to what the Spirit is declaring to the churches. The person who conquers will suffer no harm whatsoever from the second death.’
    <verse eid="REV 2:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">To the Church in Pergamum</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="REV 2:12"/>
    “To the angel or messenger of the church in Pergamum, write:
    <verse eid="REV 2:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“These are the declarations of the One who wields the sharp sword with two edges:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="REV 2:13"/>
    ‘I have full knowledge of where you dwell—in the very location where Satan has established his throne. Yet you cling firmly to My name and did not renounce your faith in Me, even during the time when Antipas, My faithful witness, was martyred among you, in the place where Satan resides.
    <verse eid="REV 2:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="REV 2:14"/>
    However, I have a few complaints against you: You have some members there who embrace the teaching of Balaam, who instructed Balak how to cause the Israelites to stumble by enticing them to eat food sacrificed to idols and to engage in sexual immorality.
    <verse eid="REV 2:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="REV 2:15"/>
    Likewise, you have some who hold to the teaching of the Nicolaitans.
    <verse eid="REV 2:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="REV 2:16"/>
    Therefore repent. But if you refuse, I will come to you swiftly and will make war against them using the sword that comes from My mouth.
    <verse eid="REV 2:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="REV 2:17"/>
    ‘Let anyone who has ears pay close attention to what the Spirit is declaring to the churches. To the person who conquers, I will give a portion of the hidden manna. I will also give that person a white stone inscribed with a new name that no one understands except the one who receives it.’
    <verse eid="REV 2:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">To the Church in Thyatira</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="REV 2:18"/>
    “To the angel or messenger of the church in Thyatira, write:
    <verse eid="REV 2:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“These are the declarations of the Son of God, whose eyes blaze like flames of fire and whose feet gleam like refined bronze:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="REV 2:19"/>
    ‘I have full knowledge of your deeds—your love, your faith, your service, and your patient endurance. I know that your recent deeds surpass your earlier ones.
    <verse eid="REV 2:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="REV 2:20"/>
    Nevertheless, I hold this charge against you: You are permitting that woman Jezebel, who designates herself a prophetess, to teach and seduce My servants into committing sexual immorality and eating food sacrificed to idols.
    <verse eid="REV 2:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="REV 2:21"/>
    I have granted her time to repent, but she refuses to turn away from her sexual immorality.
    <verse eid="REV 2:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="REV 2:22"/>
    Take notice. I am about to throw her onto a bed of anguish, and I will plunge those who commit adultery with her into severe tribulation, unless they repent of their participation in her deeds.
    <verse eid="REV 2:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="REV 2:23"/>
    I will strike her followers dead with plague, and all the churches will recognize that I am the One who examines innermost thoughts and desires, and I will repay each of you according to your actions.
    <verse eid="REV 2:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="REV 2:24"/>
    ‘But to the rest of you in Thyatira—all of you who do not embrace this teaching and have not explored what some people call Satan’s deep secrets—I say that I will impose no additional burden on you.
    <verse eid="REV 2:24"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="REV 2:25"/>
    However, hold tightly to what you possess until I arrive.
    <verse eid="REV 2:25"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="REV 2:26"/>
    To the person who conquers and continues performing My works until the end, I will grant authority over the nations.
    <verse eid="REV 2:26"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="REV 2:27"/>
    That person will rule them with an iron rod and will shatter them like clay pottery—exactly as I have received authority from My Father.
    <verse eid="REV 2:27"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="REV 2:28"/>
    I will also give that person the morning star.
    <verse eid="REV 2:28"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="REV 2:29"/>
    ‘Let anyone who has ears pay close attention to what the Spirit is declaring to the churches.’
    <verse eid="REV 2:29"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="REV 2"/>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="REV 3"/>
  <para style="s1">To the Church in Sardis</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="REV 3:1"/>
    “To the angel or messenger of the church in Sardis, write:
    <verse eid="REV 3:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“These are the declarations of the One who possesses the seven Spirits of God and the seven stars: </para>
  <para style="p">‘I have complete knowledge of your deeds. You possess a reputation for being spiritually alive, but in reality you are spiritually dead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="REV 3:2"/>
    Awaken and fortify what little remains that is about to die, for I have determined that your deeds are incomplete in the sight of My God.
    <verse eid="REV 3:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="REV 3:3"/>
    Remember what you originally received and heard; guard it carefully and repent. But if you fail to wake up, I will arrive like a thief, and you will have absolutely no idea at what hour I will come upon you.
    <verse eid="REV 3:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="REV 3:4"/>
    ‘Yet you have a few individuals in Sardis who have not contaminated their garments. They will walk alongside Me dressed in white because they have proven themselves worthy.
    <verse eid="REV 3:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="REV 3:5"/>
    The person who conquers will similarly be clothed in white garments, and I will absolutely never erase that person’s name from the book of life. Rather, I will openly acknowledge that name in the presence of My Father and in the presence of His angels.
    <verse eid="REV 3:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="REV 3:6"/>
    ‘Let anyone who has ears pay close attention to what the Spirit is declaring to the churches.’
    <verse eid="REV 3:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">To the Church in Philadelphia</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="REV 3:7"/>
    “To the angel or messenger of the church in Philadelphia, write:
    <verse eid="REV 3:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“These are the declarations of the Holy One, the True One, who holds the key of David. What He opens, no one can close, and what He closes, no one can open:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="REV 3:8"/>
    ‘I have complete knowledge of your deeds. Take notice! I have set before you an open door that no one has the power to close. I recognize that you possess only limited strength, yet you have obeyed My word and have not denied My name.
    <verse eid="REV 3:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="REV 3:9"/>
    Pay attention! I will deal with those who belong to Satan’s synagogue—those who falsely claim to be Jews when they are actually lying—indeed, I will make them come and prostrate themselves at your feet and acknowledge that I have loved you.
    <verse eid="REV 3:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="REV 3:10"/>
    Because you have obeyed My commandment to endure patiently, I will likewise protect you from the hour of testing that is about to come upon the entire world to test those who inhabit the earth.
    <verse eid="REV 3:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="REV 3:11"/>
    ‘I am coming soon. Grasp tightly what you possess, so that no one seizes your victor's crown.
    <verse eid="REV 3:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="REV 3:12"/>
    The person who conquers I will establish as a pillar in the temple of My God, and that person will never depart from it again. I will inscribe on that person the name of My God and the name of the city of My God—the new Jerusalem descending out of heaven from My God—and My own new name.
    <verse eid="REV 3:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="REV 3:13"/>
    ‘Let anyone who has ears pay close attention to what the Spirit is declaring to the churches.’
    <verse eid="REV 3:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">To the Church in Laodicea</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="REV 3:14"/>
    “To the angel or messenger of the church in Laodicea, write:
    <verse eid="REV 3:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“These are the declarations of the Amen, the faithful and true Witness, the Source of God’s creation:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="REV 3:15"/>
    ‘I have complete knowledge of your deeds—you are neither spiritually cold nor spiritually hot. I wish you were one or the other!
    <verse eid="REV 3:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="REV 3:16"/>
    So because you are lukewarm, neither hot nor cold, I am about to vomit you out of My mouth.
    <verse eid="REV 3:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="REV 3:17"/>
    ‘You keep saying, “I am wealthy and have acquired riches and need nothing,” but you fail to realize that you are miserable, pitiful, poverty-stricken, blind, and naked.
    <verse eid="REV 3:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="REV 3:18"/>
    I advise you to purchase from Me gold refined through fire so that you may become genuinely wealthy, and white garments so that you may be properly clothed and the shameful exposure of your nakedness will not be revealed, and salve to apply to your eyes so that you may see clearly.
    <verse eid="REV 3:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="REV 3:19"/>
    ‘All those whom I love I correct and discipline. Therefore become zealous and repent.
    <verse eid="REV 3:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="REV 3:20"/>
    Pay attention! I stand at the door knocking. If anyone hears My voice and opens the door, I will enter and share a meal with that person, and that person with Me.
    <verse eid="REV 3:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="REV 3:21"/>
    To the person who conquers, I will grant the privilege of sitting down with Me on My throne, just as I conquered and sat down with My Father on His throne.
    <verse eid="REV 3:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="REV 3:22"/>
    ‘Let anyone who has ears pay close attention to what the Spirit is declaring to the churches.’ ”
    <verse eid="REV 3:22"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="REV 3"/>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="REV 4"/>
  <para style="s1">Vision of the Heavenly Throne</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="REV 4:1"/>
    After these things I looked, and there before me stood an open door in heaven. The first voice I had heard speaking to me like a trumpet said, “Come here, and I will reveal to you what must happen after these present events.”
    <verse eid="REV 4:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="REV 4:2"/>
    Instantly I was in the Spirit, and there before me stood a throne in heaven with Someone seated on the throne.
    <verse eid="REV 4:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="REV 4:3"/>
    The One sitting there had an appearance resembling jasper and carnelian stones, and encircling the throne was a rainbow with an appearance like emerald.
    <verse eid="REV 4:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="REV 4:4"/>
    Surrounding that throne were twenty-four additional thrones, and seated on those thrones were twenty-four elders dressed in white garments with golden crowns on their heads.
    <verse eid="REV 4:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="REV 4:5"/>
    From the throne emanated lightning flashes, rumblings, and peals of thunder. Seven blazing lamps were burning before the throne, which represent the seven Spirits of God.
    <verse eid="REV 4:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="REV 4:6"/>
    Extending before the throne was something resembling a sea of glass, transparent as crystal.
    <verse eid="REV 4:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">At the very center and surrounding the throne, were four living beings, covered with eyes both in front and behind.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="REV 4:7"/>
    The first living being resembled a lion, the second living being resembled an ox, the third living being possessed a face like a man, and the fourth living being resembled an eagle in flight.
    <verse eid="REV 4:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="REV 4:8"/>
    Each of the four living beings had six wings and was covered with eyes all around and underneath. Day and night they never cease declaring,
    <verse eid="REV 4:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Holy, holy, holy is the Lord God Almighty,</para>
  <para style="p">who existed in the past, who exists now, and who will come in the future.”</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="REV 4:9"/>
    Whenever the living beings ascribe glory, honor, and thanksgiving to the One seated on the throne—the One who lives throughout all the ages,
    <verse eid="REV 4:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="REV 4:10"/>
    the twenty-four elders prostrate themselves before the One seated on the throne and worship the One who lives throughout all the ages. They cast their crowns before the throne and declare,
    <verse eid="REV 4:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="REV 4:11"/>
    “You are worthy, our Lord and God,
    <verse eid="REV 4:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">to receive glory and honor and power,</para>
  <para style="p">for You created all things,</para>
  <para style="p">and because of Your will they existed and were brought into being.”</para>
  <chapter eid="REV 4"/>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="REV 5"/>
  <para style="s1">The Lamb and the Scroll with Seven Seals</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="REV 5:1"/>
    Then I observed in the right hand of the One seated on the throne a scroll with writing on both the inside and the back, sealed with seven seals.
    <verse eid="REV 5:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="REV 5:2"/>
    I saw a mighty angel proclaiming in a thunderous voice, “Who is worthy to break the seals and open the scroll?”
    <verse eid="REV 5:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="REV 5:3"/>
    But no one in heaven or on earth or beneath the earth had the power to open the scroll or examine its contents.
    <verse eid="REV 5:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="REV 5:4"/>
    I began weeping profusely because no one was found worthy to open the scroll or examine it.
    <verse eid="REV 5:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="REV 5:5"/>
    Then one of the elders said to me, “Stop weeping! Look—the Lion from the tribe of Judah, the Root of David, has conquered and is therefore able to open the scroll and its seven seals.”
    <verse eid="REV 5:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="REV 5:6"/>
    Then I saw standing in the center of the throne, surrounded by the four living beings and the elders, a Lamb that appeared as though it had been slaughtered. It possessed seven horns and seven eyes, which represent the seven Spirits of God dispatched into all the earth.
    <verse eid="REV 5:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="REV 5:7"/>
    He approached and took the scroll from the right hand of the One seated on the throne.
    <verse eid="REV 5:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="REV 5:8"/>
    When He had taken the scroll, the four living beings and the twenty-four elders prostrated themselves before the Lamb. Each one held a harp and golden bowls brimming with incense, which represent the prayers of the saints.
    <verse eid="REV 5:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="REV 5:9"/>
    They sang a new song with these words:
    <verse eid="REV 5:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“You are worthy to take the scroll and to break its seals,</para>
  <para style="p">because You were slaughtered,</para>
  <para style="p">and with Your blood You purchased people for God</para>
  <para style="p">from every tribe and language </para>
  <para style="p">and people group and nation.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="REV 5:10"/>
    You have constituted them as a kingdom and priests to serve our God,
    <verse eid="REV 5:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">and they will reign on the earth.”</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="REV 5:11"/>
    Then I looked and heard the voices of countless angels encircling the throne, the living beings, and the elders. Their number was myriads upon myriads and thousands upon thousands.
    <verse eid="REV 5:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="REV 5:12"/>
    They proclaimed in a mighty voice,
    <verse eid="REV 5:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Worthy is the Lamb who was slaughtered</para>
  <para style="p">to receive power and wealth and wisdom and strength</para>
  <para style="p">and honor and glory and praise!”</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="REV 5:13"/>
    Then I heard every creature in heaven and on earth and beneath the earth and on the sea—all that exists within them—declaring:
    <verse eid="REV 5:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“To the One seated on the throne and to the Lamb</para>
  <para style="p">be praise and honor and glory and dominion</para>
  <para style="p">throughout all the ages!”</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="REV 5:14"/>
    The four living beings responded, “Amen!” And the elders prostrated themselves and worshipped.
    <verse eid="REV 5:14"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="REV 5"/>
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="REV 6"/>
  <para style="s1">First Seal: The White Horse and the Conqueror</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="REV 6:1"/>
    I watched as the Lamb broke one of the seven seals, and I heard one of the four living beings say with a voice like thunder, “Come!”
    <verse eid="REV 6:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="REV 6:2"/>
    I looked, and there before me appeared a white horse! Its rider carried a bow, and a crown was placed on his head. He rode out as a conqueror determined to conquer.
    <verse eid="REV 6:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Second Seal: The Fiery Red Horse and the Destroyer</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="REV 6:3"/>
    When the Lamb opened the second seal, I heard the second living being say, “Come!”
    <verse eid="REV 6:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="REV 6:4"/>
    Then another horse came forth, fiery red in color. Its rider was authorized to remove peace from the earth and to make people slaughter one another. He was given a large sword.
    <verse eid="REV 6:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Third Seal: The Black Horse and Famine on Earth</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="REV 6:5"/>
    When the Lamb opened the third seal, I heard the third living being say, “Come!” I looked, and there before me appeared a black horse! Its rider was holding a pair of scales in his hand.
    <verse eid="REV 6:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="REV 6:6"/>
    Then I heard what seemed to be a voice coming from among the four living beings, announcing, “A quart of wheat for a day’s wages, and three quarts of barley for a day’s wages, but do not damage the olive oil and the wine!”
    <verse eid="REV 6:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Fourth Seal: The Pale Green Horse and Death and Hades</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="REV 6:7"/>
    When the Lamb opened the fourth seal, I heard the voice of the fourth living being say, “Come!”
    <verse eid="REV 6:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="REV 6:8"/>
    I looked, and there before me appeared a pale green horse! Its rider was named Death, and Hades followed close behind him. They were granted authority over one-fourth of the earth to kill by sword, famine, plague, and by the wild animals of the earth.
    <verse eid="REV 6:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Fifth Seal: The Loud Cries of the Martyrs</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="REV 6:9"/>
    When He opened the fifth seal, I saw beneath the altar the souls of those who had been slaughtered because they had proclaimed God’s word and because they had maintained their faithful testimony.
    <verse eid="REV 6:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="REV 6:10"/>
    They cried out in a loud voice, “How long, holy and true Sovereign Lord, until You judge the inhabitants of the earth and avenge our blood?”
    <verse eid="REV 6:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="REV 6:11"/>
    Then each of them was given a white robe, and they were instructed to rest a little longer, until the complete number of their fellow servants and brothers and sisters who were destined to be killed just as they had been was reached.
    <verse eid="REV 6:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Sixth Seal: Cosmic Catastrophes</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="REV 6:12"/>
    I watched as He opened the sixth seal, and a massive earthquake occurred. The sun turned black like coarse sackcloth made from goat hair, and the entire moon became like blood.
    <verse eid="REV 6:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="REV 6:13"/>
    The stars of the sky fell to the earth like a fig tree drops its late figs when shaken by a violent wind.
    <verse eid="REV 6:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="REV 6:14"/>
    The sky split apart like a scroll being rolled up, and every mountain and island was displaced from its location.
    <verse eid="REV 6:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="REV 6:15"/>
    Then the kings of the earth, the nobility, the military commanders, the wealthy, the powerful, and every slave and free person hid themselves in caves and among the rocks of the mountains.
    <verse eid="REV 6:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="REV 6:16"/>
    They called out to the mountains and the rocks, “Fall on us and conceal us from the face of the One seated on the throne and from the wrath of the Lamb!
    <verse eid="REV 6:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="REV 6:17"/>
    For the great day of Their wrath has arrived, and who has the ability to withstand it?”
    <verse eid="REV 6:17"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="REV 6"/>
  <chapter number="7" style="c" sid="REV 7"/>
  <para style="s1">The Sealing of the 144,000 of Israel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="REV 7:1"/>
    After this I saw four angels standing at the four corners of the earth, restraining the four winds of the earth so that no wind would blow on the land or on the sea or on any tree.
    <verse eid="REV 7:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="REV 7:2"/>
    Then I saw another angel ascending from the east, carrying the seal of the living God. He shouted in a loud voice to the four angels who had been authorized to damage the land and the sea,
    <verse eid="REV 7:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="REV 7:3"/>
    declaring, “Do not damage the land or the sea or the trees until we have sealed the servants of our God on their foreheads.”
    <verse eid="REV 7:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="REV 7:4"/>
    Then I heard the number of those who were sealed: 144,000 sealed from every tribe of the descendants of Israel:
    <verse eid="REV 7:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="REV 7:5"/>
    From the tribe of Judah, 12,000 were sealed,
    <verse eid="REV 7:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">from the tribe of Reuben, 12,000,</para>
  <para style="p">from the tribe of Gad, 12,000,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="REV 7:6"/>
    from the tribe of Asher, 12,000,
    <verse eid="REV 7:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">from the tribe of Naphtali, 12,000,</para>
  <para style="p">from the tribe of Manasseh, 12,000,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="REV 7:7"/>
    from the tribe of Simeon, 12,000,
    <verse eid="REV 7:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">from the tribe of Levi, 12,000,</para>
  <para style="p">from the tribe of Issachar, 12,000,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="REV 7:8"/>
    from the tribe of Zebulun, 12,000,
    <verse eid="REV 7:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">from the tribe of Joseph, 12,000,</para>
  <para style="p">from the tribe of Benjamin, 12,000 were sealed.</para>
  <para style="s1">A Great Multitude of Believers from All Nations</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="REV 7:9"/>
    After this I looked, and there before me was an enormous multitude that no one could count, from every nation, tribe, people group, and language, standing before the throne and before the Lamb. They were clothed in white robes and held palm branches in their hands.
    <verse eid="REV 7:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="REV 7:10"/>
    They shouted in a loud voice,
    <verse eid="REV 7:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Salvation belongs to our God,</para>
  <para style="p">who sits on the throne,</para>
  <para style="p">and to the Lamb!”</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="REV 7:11"/>
    All the angels were standing in a circle around the throne, around the elders, and around the four living beings. They prostrated themselves face-down before the throne and worshipped God,
    <verse eid="REV 7:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="REV 7:12"/>
    declaring,
    <verse eid="REV 7:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Amen!</para>
  <para style="p">Praise and glory</para>
  <para style="p">and wisdom and thanksgiving and honor</para>
  <para style="p">and power and strength</para>
  <para style="p">belong to our God throughout all the ages. Amen!”</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="REV 7:13"/>
    Then one of the elders addressed me, asking, “These people clothed in white robes—who are they, and where did they come from?”
    <verse eid="REV 7:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="REV 7:14"/>
    I responded, “Sir, you are the one who knows.” He said to me, “These are the ones who have emerged from the great tribulation. They have washed their robes and made them white in the blood of the Lamb.
    <verse eid="REV 7:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="REV 7:15"/>
    For this reason, they stand before God’s throne
    <verse eid="REV 7:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">and serve Him day and night in His temple sanctuary;</para>
  <para style="p">and the One who sits on the throne will spread His tabernacle over them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="REV 7:16"/>
    They will never hunger again;
    <verse eid="REV 7:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">they will never thirst again.</para>
  <para style="p">The sun will never beat down on them,</para>
  <para style="p">nor any scorching heat.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="REV 7:17"/>
    For the Lamb at the center of the throne will shepherd them
    <verse eid="REV 7:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">and will guide them to springs of living water,</para>
  <para style="p">and God will wipe away every tear from their eyes.”</para>
  <chapter eid="REV 7"/>
  <chapter number="8" style="c" sid="REV 8"/>
  <para style="s1">The Seventh Seal and the Golden Censer</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="REV 8:1"/>
    When He opened the seventh seal, silence fell over heaven for approximately half an hour.
    <verse eid="REV 8:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="REV 8:2"/>
    Then I saw the seven angels who stand in God’s presence, and seven trumpets were given to them.
    <verse eid="REV 8:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="REV 8:3"/>
    Another angel, holding a golden censer, came and stood at the altar. He was given a large quantity of incense to offer, along with the prayers of all the saints, on the golden altar that was set before the throne.
    <verse eid="REV 8:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="REV 8:4"/>
    The smoke of the incense, mingled with the prayers of the saints, ascended from the angel's hand into God’s presence.
    <verse eid="REV 8:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="REV 8:5"/>
    Then the angel took the censer, filled it with fire from the altar, and hurled it down upon the earth. There followed peals of thunder, rumblings, lightning flashes, and an earthquake.
    <verse eid="REV 8:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Trumpets</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="REV 8:6"/>
    Then the seven angels holding the seven trumpets prepared themselves to sound them.
    <verse eid="REV 8:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">First Trumpet: The Burning of Vegetation</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="REV 8:7"/>
    The first angel sounded his trumpet, and hail and fire mixed with blood came down and was hurled upon the earth. One-third of the earth was burned up, one-third of the trees were burned up, and all the green grass was burned up.
    <verse eid="REV 8:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Second Trumpet: The Sea Struck</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="REV 8:8"/>
    The second angel sounded his trumpet, and something resembling an enormous mountain blazing with fire was hurled into the sea. One-third of the sea turned into blood,
    <verse eid="REV 8:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="REV 8:9"/>
    one-third of the living creatures in the sea died, and one-third of the ships were destroyed.
    <verse eid="REV 8:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Third Trumpet: The Waters Struck</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="REV 8:10"/>
    The third angel sounded his trumpet, and a great star blazing like a torch fell from the sky. It fell on one-third of the rivers and on the springs of water.
    <verse eid="REV 8:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="REV 8:11"/>
    The name of the star is Wormwood. One-third of the waters became bitter like wormwood, and many people died from drinking the waters that had become bitter.
    <verse eid="REV 8:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Fourth Trumpet: The Striking of the Sun, Moon, and Stars</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="REV 8:12"/>
    The fourth angel sounded his trumpet, and one-third of the sun was struck, one-third of the moon, and one-third of the stars, so that one-third of them became dark. One-third of the day lost its light, and likewise one-third of the night.
    <verse eid="REV 8:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="REV 8:13"/>
    As I watched, I heard an eagle flying through midair, crying out in a loud voice, “Horror, horror, horror awaits the inhabitants of the earth because of the remaining trumpet blasts that the three angels are about to sound!”
    <verse eid="REV 8:13"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="REV 8"/>
  <chapter number="9" style="c" sid="REV 9"/>
  <para style="s1">Fifth Trumpet: The Emergence of the Locusts from the Bottomless Pit</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="REV 9:1"/>
    The fifth angel sounded his trumpet, and I saw a star that had fallen from the sky to the earth. The star was given the key to the shaft leading to the bottomless pit.
    <verse eid="REV 9:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="REV 9:2"/>
    When he opened the shaft, smoke billowed up from it like smoke from a gigantic furnace. The sun and the atmosphere were darkened by the smoke from the shaft.
    <verse eid="REV 9:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="REV 9:3"/>
    Out of the smoke, locusts descended upon the earth, and they were given power like the power that scorpions of the earth possess.
    <verse eid="REV 9:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="REV 9:4"/>
    They were instructed not to damage the grass of the earth or any plant or tree, but only those people who did not have God’s seal on their foreheads.
    <verse eid="REV 9:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="REV 9:5"/>
    The locusts were not authorized to kill them but only to torment them for five months. Their torment was like the agony caused by a scorpion when it stings a person.
    <verse eid="REV 9:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="REV 9:6"/>
    During those days people will seek death but will never find it; they will long to die, but death will elude them.
    <verse eid="REV 9:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="REV 9:7"/>
    The appearance of the locusts was like horses prepared for battle. On their heads they wore what appeared to be crowns resembling gold, and their faces looked like human faces.
    <verse eid="REV 9:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="REV 9:8"/>
    Their hair was like women’s hair, and their teeth were like lions' teeth.
    <verse eid="REV 9:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="REV 9:9"/>
    They had breastplates that looked like breastplates of iron, and the sound of their wings was like the thundering of many horses and chariots charging into battle.
    <verse eid="REV 9:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="REV 9:10"/>
    They possessed tails with stingers like scorpions, and in their tails was their power to inflict pain on people for five months.
    <verse eid="REV 9:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="REV 9:11"/>
    Ruling over them as king was the angel of the bottomless pit, whose name in Hebrew is Abaddon, and in Greek his name is Apollyon.
    <verse eid="REV 9:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="REV 9:12"/>
    The first catastrophe has passed; two more catastrophes are still coming.
    <verse eid="REV 9:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Sixth Trumpet: The Release of the Angels Bound at the Euphrates</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="REV 9:13"/>
    The sixth angel sounded his trumpet, and I heard a voice emanating from the four horns of the golden altar that stands before God.
    <verse eid="REV 9:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="REV 9:14"/>
    The voice said to the sixth angel who held the trumpet, “Release the four angels who are bound at the great river Euphrates.”
    <verse eid="REV 9:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="REV 9:15"/>
    So the four angels who had been kept ready for this precise hour, day, month, and year were released to kill one-third of humanity.
    <verse eid="REV 9:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="REV 9:16"/>
    The number of mounted troops was two hundred million. I heard their number.
    <verse eid="REV 9:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="REV 9:17"/>
    In my vision I saw the horses and their riders: They wore breastplates that were fiery red, dark blue, and sulfur yellow. The heads of the horses resembled lions’ heads, and from their mouths came fire, smoke, and sulfur.
    <verse eid="REV 9:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="REV 9:18"/>
    One-third of humanity was killed by these three plagues—by the fire, the smoke, and the sulfur pouring from their mouths.
    <verse eid="REV 9:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="REV 9:19"/>
    For the power of the horses was located in their mouths and in their tails; their tails were like serpents, equipped with heads, and with them they inflict injury.
    <verse eid="REV 9:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="REV 9:20"/>
    The rest of humanity who were not killed by these plagues still refused to repent of the works of their hands. They did not stop worshipping demons and idols made of gold, silver, bronze, stone, and wood—idols that cannot see or hear or walk.
    <verse eid="REV 9:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="REV 9:21"/>
    They did not repent of their murders, their sorcery, their sexual immorality, or their thefts.
    <verse eid="REV 9:21"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="REV 9"/>
  <chapter number="10" style="c" sid="REV 10"/>
  <para style="s1">The Mighty Angel and the Little Scroll</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="REV 10:1"/>
    Then I saw another mighty angel descending from heaven. He was wrapped in a cloud, with a rainbow over his head. His face shone like the sun, and his legs were like pillars of fire.
    <verse eid="REV 10:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="REV 10:2"/>
    He was holding a small scroll that lay open in his hand. He placed his right foot on the sea and his left foot on the land.
    <verse eid="REV 10:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="REV 10:3"/>
    Then he shouted with a loud voice like a lion roaring. When he shouted, the seven thunders spoke with their own voices.
    <verse eid="REV 10:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="REV 10:4"/>
    When the seven thunders had spoken, I was about to write, but I heard a voice from heaven saying, “Seal up what the seven thunders have said and do not write it down.”
    <verse eid="REV 10:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="REV 10:5"/>
    Then the angel I had seen standing on the sea and on the land raised his right hand toward heaven.
    <verse eid="REV 10:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="REV 10:6"/>
    He swore an oath by the One who lives throughout all the ages, who created heaven and everything in it, the earth and everything in it, and the sea and everything in it: “There will be no more delay!
    <verse eid="REV 10:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="REV 10:7"/>
    But in the days when the seventh angel is about to sound his trumpet, God’s mysterious plan will be fulfilled, just as He announced to His servants the prophets.”
    <verse eid="REV 10:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="REV 10:8"/>
    Then the voice I had heard from heaven spoke to me again: “Go, take the scroll that lies open in the hand of the angel who is standing on the sea and on the land.”
    <verse eid="REV 10:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="REV 10:9"/>
    So I approached the angel and asked him to give me the small scroll. He said to me, “Take it and eat it completely. It will make your stomach bitter, but in your mouth it will taste as sweet as honey.”
    <verse eid="REV 10:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="REV 10:10"/>
    I took the small scroll from the angel’s hand and ate it completely. In my mouth it tasted as sweet as honey, but when I had swallowed it, my stomach turned bitter.
    <verse eid="REV 10:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="REV 10:11"/>
    And I was told, “You must prophesy again concerning many peoples, nations, languages, and kings.”
    <verse eid="REV 10:11"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="REV 10"/>
  <chapter number="11" style="c" sid="REV 11"/>
  <para style="s1">The Two Prophetic Witnesses</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="REV 11:1"/>
    Then a reed resembling a staff was given to me, and someone said, “Get up and measure God’s temple sanctuary and the altar, and count those who are worshipping there.
    <verse eid="REV 11:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="REV 11:2"/>
    But leave the outer courtyard unmeasured and excluded, for it has been handed over to the Gentile nations, and they will trample the holy city underfoot for forty-two months.
    <verse eid="REV 11:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="REV 11:3"/>
    I will commission My two witnesses, and they will proclaim God’s message for 1,260 days while dressed in sackcloth.”
    <verse eid="REV 11:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="REV 11:4"/>
    These two witnesses are the two olive trees and the two lampstands that stand in the presence of the Lord who rules the earth.
    <verse eid="REV 11:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="REV 11:5"/>
    If anyone attempts to harm them, fire pours out from their mouths and consumes their adversaries. Yes, if anyone wants to harm them, this is how that person must die.
    <verse eid="REV 11:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="REV 11:6"/>
    These witnesses possess authority to shut the sky so that no rain falls during the period of their prophetic ministry. They also possess authority to turn the waters into blood and to strike the earth with any plague whenever they choose.
    <verse eid="REV 11:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="REV 11:7"/>
    When they complete their testimony, the beast that rises out of the abyss will wage war against them and will conquer them and put them to death.
    <verse eid="REV 11:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="REV 11:8"/>
    Their corpses will lie in the public street of the great city that is spiritually identified as Sodom and Egypt—the same place where their Lord was crucified.
    <verse eid="REV 11:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="REV 11:9"/>
    People from various nations, tribes, languages, and ethnic groups will stare at their corpses for three and a half days and will refuse to permit their bodies to be placed in a tomb.
    <verse eid="REV 11:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="REV 11:10"/>
    The earth’s inhabitants will rejoice over them and celebrate and exchange gifts with one another, because these two prophets had brought torment to those living on the earth.
    <verse eid="REV 11:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="REV 11:11"/>
    But after three and a half days, the breath of life from God entered them, and they stood upright on their feet. Great terror seized those watching them.
    <verse eid="REV 11:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="REV 11:12"/>
    Then they heard a powerful voice from heaven calling to them, “Come up here!” And they ascended into heaven in a cloud while their enemies watched them go.
    <verse eid="REV 11:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="REV 11:13"/>
    In that same hour, a violent earthquake struck, and one-tenth of the city collapsed. Seven thousand individuals perished in the earthquake, and the rest were filled with fear and gave glory to the God of heaven.
    <verse eid="REV 11:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="REV 11:14"/>
    The second catastrophe has ended; the third catastrophe is approaching quickly.
    <verse eid="REV 11:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Seventh Trumpet</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="REV 11:15"/>
    Then the seventh angel blew his trumpet, and loud voices rang out in heaven, proclaiming,
    <verse eid="REV 11:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“The kingdom of this world has now become</para>
  <para style="p">the kingdom of our Lord and of His Christ,</para>
  <para style="p">and He will reign throughout all the ages to come.”</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="REV 11:16"/>
    Then the twenty-four elders who sit on their thrones in God’s presence prostrated themselves face-down and worshiped God,
    <verse eid="REV 11:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="REV 11:17"/>
    declaring:
    <verse eid="REV 11:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“We give You thanks, Lord God Almighty,</para>
  <para style="p">the One who exists now and who has always existed,</para>
  <para style="p">because You have seized Your great power</para>
  <para style="p">and have assumed Your reign.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="REV 11:18"/>
    The nations raged in fury,
    <verse eid="REV 11:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">but Your wrath has arrived,</para>
  <para style="p">along with the appointed time for the dead to be judged,</para>
  <para style="p">the time to grant rewards to Your servants the prophets</para>
  <para style="p">and to the saints</para>
  <para style="p">and to all who fear Your name,</para>
  <para style="p">whether insignificant or influential—</para>
  <para style="p">and the time to destroy those who are destroying the earth.”</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="REV 11:19"/>
    Then God’s temple in heaven was opened, and the ark of His covenant became visible inside His temple. There followed lightning flashes, rumblings, peals of thunder, an earthquake, and a violent hailstorm.
    <verse eid="REV 11:19"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="REV 11"/>
  <chapter number="12" style="c" sid="REV 12"/>
  <para style="s1">The Woman, the Child, and the Dragon</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="REV 12:1"/>
    A striking vision appeared in heaven: A woman clothed in radiant light like the sun, standing upon the moon, and crowned with twelve stars.
    <verse eid="REV 12:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="REV 12:2"/>
    She was pregnant and cried out in the agony of labor.
    <verse eid="REV 12:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="REV 12:3"/>
    Another sign appeared: A massive red dragon, terrifying in appearance, with seven heads and ten horns, each head crowned.
    <verse eid="REV 12:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="REV 12:4"/>
    With a sweep of his tail he hurled a third of the stars from the sky down to the earth. He stationed himself before the woman, waiting to devour her Child as soon as He was born.
    <verse eid="REV 12:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="REV 12:5"/>
    She gave birth to a Son—a male Child—destined to rule the nations with unbreakable authority. But the Child was caught up to God and to His throne.
    <verse eid="REV 12:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="REV 12:6"/>
    The woman fled into the wilderness, to a place God had prepared, where she would be sustained for 1,260 days.
    <verse eid="REV 12:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Satan and His Angels Cast Out of Heaven</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="REV 12:7"/>
    A war broke out in heaven: Michael and his angels fought against the dragon. The dragon and his angels resisted,
    <verse eid="REV 12:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="REV 12:8"/>
    but they were overpowered and expelled; there was no longer any place for them in heaven.
    <verse eid="REV 12:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="REV 12:9"/>
    The great dragon—the ancient serpent known as the devil and Satan, the deceiver of the whole world—was cast down to the earth, and his angels were thrown down with him.
    <verse eid="REV 12:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="REV 12:10"/>
    Then a loud declaration resounded in heaven: “Now salvation, power, and the kingdom of our God have been established, and the authority of His Christ is revealed. The accuser of our brothers and sisters has been cast down—the one who constantly accused them before God.
    <verse eid="REV 12:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="REV 12:11"/>
    They overcame him through the blood of the Lamb and through their faithful testimony; they did not cling to life, even in the face of death.
    <verse eid="REV 12:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="REV 12:12"/>
    Therefore rejoice, O heavens! But disaster looms over the earth and sea, for the devil has come down in fury, aware that his time is limited.”
    <verse eid="REV 12:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Satan Pursues the Woman and Engages in War with Her Children</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="REV 12:13"/>
    Realizing he had been cast to earth, the dragon pursued the woman who had given birth to the male Child.
    <verse eid="REV 12:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="REV 12:14"/>
    But she was given the two wings of the great eagle to escape swiftly into the wilderness, where she was sustained for a time, and times, and half a time, beyond the serpent’s reach.
    <verse eid="REV 12:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="REV 12:15"/>
    The serpent spewed out a torrent like a river to sweep her away,
    <verse eid="REV 12:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="REV 12:16"/>
    but the earth intervened, swallowing the flood and rescuing her.
    <verse eid="REV 12:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="REV 12:17"/>
    Enraged, the dragon turned to wage war against the rest of her offspring—those who remain obedient to God and loyal to the testimony of Jesus.
    <verse eid="REV 12:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="REV 12:18"/>
    And he stood on the sand of the seashore.
    <verse eid="REV 12:18"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="REV 12"/>
  <chapter number="13" style="c" sid="REV 13"/>
  <para style="s1">The Beast from the Sea</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="REV 13:1"/>
    From the sea I saw a beast emerge, bearing ten horns and seven heads. And on his horns were ten crowns, and blasphemous names marked his heads.
    <verse eid="REV 13:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="REV 13:2"/>
    He resembled a leopard, with feet like a bear and a mouth like a lion. The dragon granted him his power, his throne, and sweeping authority.
    <verse eid="REV 13:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="REV 13:3"/>
    One of his heads appeared fatally wounded, yet the wound had been healed. The world was astonished and followed him.
    <verse eid="REV 13:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="REV 13:4"/>
    People worshipped the dragon for empowering the beast, and they worshipped the beast, saying, “Who can compare to him? Who can defeat him?”
    <verse eid="REV 13:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="REV 13:5"/>
    He was allowed to speak arrogant and blasphemous words and to exercise authority for forty-two months.
    <verse eid="REV 13:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="REV 13:6"/>
    He uttered blasphemies against God—His name, His dwelling, and those who belong to heaven.
    <verse eid="REV 13:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="REV 13:7"/>
    He was permitted to make war against God’s people and overcome them, and he was granted authority over every people group and nation.
    <verse eid="REV 13:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="REV 13:8"/>
    All inhabitants of the earth will render worship to him—every person whose name has not been written in the book of life belonging to the Lamb slaughtered from the foundation of the world.
    <verse eid="REV 13:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="REV 13:9"/>
    Let all who are willing to hear pay attention:
    <verse eid="REV 13:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="REV 13:10"/>
    Those destined for captivity 
    <verse eid="REV 13:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">will go into captivity; </para>
  <para style="p">those destined for death by the sword </para>
  <para style="p">will face it.</para>
  <para style="p">This calls for perseverance and steadfast faith from God’s people.</para>
  <para style="s1">The Beast Rising from the Earth</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="REV 13:11"/>
    Then I saw another beast rising from the earth. He had two horns like a lamb but spoke with the voice of a dragon.
    <verse eid="REV 13:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="REV 13:12"/>
    He operated with the full authority of the first beast and compelled the world to worship that first beast—the one whose fatal wound had been healed.
    <verse eid="REV 13:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="REV 13:13"/>
    He performed astonishing signs, even calling fire down from heaven before people’s eyes.
    <verse eid="REV 13:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="REV 13:14"/>
    Through these signs he deceived humanity, urging them to construct an image honoring the beast who was wounded by the sword and yet lived. 
    <verse eid="REV 13:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="REV 13:15"/>
    He was permitted to animate the image so that it could speak and demand death for those who refused to worship it.
    <verse eid="REV 13:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="REV 13:16"/>
    He enforced a mark upon everyone—regardless of status or wealth—on the right hand or forehead,
    <verse eid="REV 13:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="REV 13:17"/>
    making participation in commerce impossible without this mark, which represented the beast’s name or number.
    <verse eid="REV 13:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="REV 13:18"/>
    This requires discernment. Whoever has insight should calculate the beast’s number, for it represents the number of a man: 666.
    <verse eid="REV 13:18"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="REV 13"/>
  <chapter number="14" style="c" sid="REV 14"/>
  <para style="s1">The Lamb and the 144,000</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="REV 14:1"/>
    I looked again and saw the Lamb standing on Mount Zion. With Him were 144,000 people who bore His name and His Father’s name written on their foreheads—openly marked as belonging to God.
    <verse eid="REV 14:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="REV 14:2"/>
    I heard a sound from heaven like the roar of many waters and like peals of thunder. The voice which I heard was like harpists skillfully playing their harps.
    <verse eid="REV 14:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="REV 14:3"/>
    They sang a new song in the presence of the throne, before the four living creatures and the elders. No one else could master this song except the 144,000—those redeemed out of the world.
    <verse eid="REV 14:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="REV 14:4"/>
    These are those who have remained spiritually pure and wholly devoted to the Lamb. They follow Him wherever He leads. Having been redeemed from among humanity, they are presented as firstfruits belonging to God and to the Lamb.
    <verse eid="REV 14:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="REV 14:5"/>
    No deceit was found in their mouths; they stand before God without accusation.
    <verse eid="REV 14:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Proclamations of the Three Angels</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="REV 14:6"/>
    Then I saw another angel flying high overhead, carrying an everlasting message of good news to proclaim to every nation, tribe, language, and people on earth.
    <verse eid="REV 14:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="REV 14:7"/>
    He cried out loudly: “Revere God and honor Him, because the time of His judgment has arrived. Worship the Creator—the One who made heaven, earth, sea, and the springs of water.”
    <verse eid="REV 14:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="REV 14:8"/>
    A second angel followed, declaring, “Babylon the great has fallen—she who caused all the nations to drink from the wine of the passion of her sexual corruption.”
    <verse eid="REV 14:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="REV 14:9"/>
    A third angel followed them, warning with a loud voice: “If anyone gives allegiance to the beast and its image, and accepts its mark on the forehead or hand,
    <verse eid="REV 14:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="REV 14:10"/>
    that person will also drink the wine of God’s fury—poured undiluted into the cup of His wrath. Such a one will face torment with fire and sulfur before the holy angels and before the Lamb.
    <verse eid="REV 14:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="REV 14:11"/>
    The smoke of their suffering rises without end, and there is no rest day or night for those who worship the beast and bear his mark.”
    <verse eid="REV 14:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="REV 14:12"/>
    This calls for the steadfast endurance of God’s people—those who obey His commandments and remain faithful to Jesus.
    <verse eid="REV 14:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="REV 14:13"/>
    Then I heard a voice from heaven instructing, “Write this: Blessed are those who die in the Lord from this time forward.”
    <verse eid="REV 14:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Yes,” says the Spirit, “they will rest from their toil, for the fruit of their faithfulness accompanies them.”</para>
  <para style="s1">The Harvest of the Earth</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="REV 14:14"/>
    I looked again and saw a white cloud, and seated upon it was one resembling a son of man. He wore a golden crown and held a sharp sickle in His hand.
    <verse eid="REV 14:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="REV 14:15"/>
    Another angel came out from the heavenly sanctuary and called out, “Swing Your sickle and reap, because the time to reap has come, for the harvest of the earth is fully ripe.”
    <verse eid="REV 14:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="REV 14:16"/>
    The One seated on the cloud swung His sickle over the earth, and the earth was harvested.
    <verse eid="REV 14:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Trampling of the Great Winepress of the Wrath of God</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="REV 14:17"/>
    Then another angel came from the heavenly temple, also holding a sharp sickle.
    <verse eid="REV 14:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="REV 14:18"/>
    Yet another angel, who had authority over fire, came from the altar and shouted to the one with the sickle: “Gather the grape clusters from the earth’s vine, because they are fully ripe.”
    <verse eid="REV 14:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="REV 14:19"/>
    The angel swung his sickle and collected the grapes of the earth, throwing them into the great winepress of God’s wrath.
    <verse eid="REV 14:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="REV 14:20"/>
    The winepress was trampled outside the city, and blood poured forth from the press, rising to the height of horses’ bridles and extending across a distance of 1,600 stadia or approximately 180 miles—portraying the overwhelming scale of judgment.
    <verse eid="REV 14:20"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="REV 14"/>
  <chapter number="15" style="c" sid="REV 15"/>
  <para style="s1">Preparation for the Bowl Judgements</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="REV 15:1"/>
    Then I saw another extraordinary sign in heaven: seven angels carrying seven final plagues. Through these, God’s wrath reaches its completion.
    <verse eid="REV 15:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="REV 15:2"/>
    I also saw something like a sea of glass, glowing with fire. Standing beside it were those who had overcome the beast, its image, and the number of its name. They held harps given by God
    <verse eid="REV 15:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="REV 15:3"/>
    and sang the song of Moses, God’s servant, and the song of the Lamb:
    <verse eid="REV 15:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Your deeds are magnificent and awe-inspiring,</para>
  <para style="p">Lord God Almighty.</para>
  <para style="p">Your ways are just and true,</para>
  <para style="p">King of the nations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="REV 15:4"/>
    Who will not fear You, Lord,
    <verse eid="REV 15:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">and glorify Your name?</para>
  <para style="p">You alone are holy.</para>
  <para style="p">All nations will come</para>
  <para style="p">and worship before You,</para>
  <para style="p">because Your righteous acts have been revealed.”</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="REV 15:5"/>
    After this, I saw the heavenly sanctuary—the tent of testimony—opened.
    <verse eid="REV 15:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="REV 15:6"/>
    The seven angels emerged from it, clothed in pure, radiant linen and wearing golden sashes across their chests.
    <verse eid="REV 15:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="REV 15:7"/>
    One of the four living creatures handed them seven golden bowls filled with the wrath of God, who lives forever.
    <verse eid="REV 15:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="REV 15:8"/>
    The sanctuary was filled with smoke from God’s glory and power, and no one could enter it until the seven plagues carried by the seven angels were completed.
    <verse eid="REV 15:8"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="REV 15"/>
  <chapter number="16" style="c" sid="REV 16"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="REV 16:1"/>
    Then I heard a powerful voice coming from the heavenly sanctuary instructing the seven angels: “Go and pour out upon the earth the seven bowls that contain the outpouring of God’s wrath.”
    <verse eid="REV 16:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The First Bowl: A Noxious and Grievous Sore</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="REV 16:2"/>
    The first angel emptied his bowl onto the earth, and painful, festering sores broke out on those who bore the beast’s mark and who had pledged allegiance to his image.
    <verse eid="REV 16:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Second Bowl: The Sea Turns into Blood</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="REV 16:3"/>
    The second angel poured his bowl into the sea, and it became like the blood of a dead person. Every living creature in the sea perished.
    <verse eid="REV 16:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Third Bowl: The Water Turns into Blood</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="REV 16:4"/>
    The third angel poured his bowl into the rivers and springs, and they too turned into blood.
    <verse eid="REV 16:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="REV 16:5"/>
    Then I heard the angel responsible for the waters declare:
    <verse eid="REV 16:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“You are just, O Eternal One—</para>
  <para style="p">You who are and who were—</para>
  <para style="p">for in these judgments You act righteously.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="REV 16:6"/>
    Because they shed the blood of Your holy people and prophets,
    <verse eid="REV 16:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">You have given them blood to drink.</para>
  <para style="p">It is what they deserve.”</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="REV 16:7"/>
    And I heard the altar or a voice from the altar affirming:
    <verse eid="REV 16:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Yes, Lord God Almighty,</para>
  <para style="p">Your judgments are true and altogether just.”</para>
  <para style="s1">The Fourth Bowl: The Sun Scorches People</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="REV 16:8"/>
    The fourth angel poured out his bowl upon the sun, and it was permitted to intensify its heat and burn people with fierce fire.
    <verse eid="REV 16:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="REV 16:9"/>
    Though they were scorched by the blazing heat, they cursed the name of God, who has authority over these plagues. Yet they refused to repent or give Him glory.
    <verse eid="REV 16:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Fifth Bowl: Darkness and Distresses</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="REV 16:10"/>
    The fifth angel poured his bowl upon the throne of the beast, plunging his realm into oppressive darkness. People writhed in anguish, biting their tongues because of their pain.
    <verse eid="REV 16:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="REV 16:11"/>
    Still they cursed the God of heaven because of their suffering and sores, and they would not turn away from their deeds.
    <verse eid="REV 16:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Sixth Bowl: The Drying up of the Euphrates</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="REV 16:12"/>
    The sixth angel poured his bowl upon the great river Euphrates, and its waters dried up, preparing the way for rulers from the east.
    <verse eid="REV 16:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="REV 16:13"/>
    Then I saw three unclean spirits, resembling frogs, coming out from the mouths of the dragon, the beast, and the false prophet.
    <verse eid="REV 16:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="REV 16:14"/>
    These were demonic spirits performing signs. They went out to the rulers of the whole world to assemble them for battle on the great day of God Almighty.
    <verse eid="REV 16:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="REV 16:15"/>
    (A voice interrupts: “See, I am coming unexpectedly, like a thief. Blessed is the one who remains alert and spiritually prepared, so that he will not be exposed in shame.”)
    <verse eid="REV 16:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="REV 16:16"/>
    And they gathered the rulers together at the place known in Hebrew as Armageddon.
    <verse eid="REV 16:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Seventh Bowl: Judgments on the Great City, Islands, Mountains, and People</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="REV 16:17"/>
    The seventh angel poured his bowl into the air, and a loud voice came from the throne in the temple declaring, “It is accomplished.”
    <verse eid="REV 16:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="REV 16:18"/>
    Suddenly brilliant lightning flashed, accompanied by rumblings, loud voices, and peals of thunder. Then a massive earthquake struck—unlike anything humanity had ever experienced since people first inhabited the earth. It was unparalleled in its intensity and destructive force. 
    <verse eid="REV 16:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="REV 16:19"/>
    The great city was torn into three sections, and the cities of the nations collapsed. God remembered Babylon the great and gave her the cup filled with the wine of His fierce wrath.
    <verse eid="REV 16:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="REV 16:20"/>
    Islands vanished, and mountains disappeared.
    <verse eid="REV 16:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="REV 16:21"/>
    Massive hailstones, each weighing about a talent, fell from the sky upon people. Yet instead of repenting, they cursed God because the plague was so devastating.
    <verse eid="REV 16:21"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="REV 16"/>
  <chapter number="17" style="c" sid="REV 17"/>
  <para style="s1">The Great Prostitute and the Beast</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="REV 17:1"/>
    Then one of the angels who had carried the bowls approached me and said, “Come, I will show you the judgment of the great prostitute who sits over many waters.
    <verse eid="REV 17:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="REV 17:2"/>
    The kings of the earth have committed sexual immorality with her, and the inhabitants of the earth have become intoxicated with the wine of her sexual corruption.”
    <verse eid="REV 17:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="REV 17:3"/>
    In the Spirit he carried me into a wilderness, where I saw a woman seated upon a scarlet beast covered with blasphemous names and possessing seven heads and ten horns.
    <verse eid="REV 17:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="REV 17:4"/>
    The woman was clothed in luxurious purple and scarlet garments and adorned with gold, jewels, and pearls. In her hand she held a golden cup filled with abominations and moral filth.
    <verse eid="REV 17:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="REV 17:5"/>
    On her forehead was written a symbolic name: “Babylon the great, mother of prostitutes and of earth’s abominations.”
    <verse eid="REV 17:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="REV 17:6"/>
    I saw that she was drunk—not with wine—but with the blood of God’s holy people and of those who bore witness to Jesus. 
    <verse eid="REV 17:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">When I saw her, I was astonished.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="REV 17:7"/>
    The angel said to me, “Why are you amazed? I will explain the mystery of the woman and of the beast that carries her, with its seven heads and ten horns.
    <verse eid="REV 17:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="REV 17:8"/>
    The beast you saw once existed, now appears absent, yet will emerge from the abyss before going to destruction. Those whose names were never written in the book of life from the world’s foundation will be astonished when they see this beast—because it once was, now is not, and yet will come. 
    <verse eid="REV 17:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="REV 17:9"/>
    This calls for wisdom. The seven heads represent seven mountains on which the woman sits, and they also signify seven rulers.
    <verse eid="REV 17:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="REV 17:10"/>
    Five have fallen, one currently reigns, and another is yet to come—and his reign will be brief.
    <verse eid="REV 17:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="REV 17:11"/>
    The beast who once was, and now is not, stands as an eighth and is headed for ruin.
    <verse eid="REV 17:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="REV 17:12"/>
    The ten horns represent ten rulers who have not yet received kingdoms, but they will receive authority for a short time alongside the beast.
    <verse eid="REV 17:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="REV 17:13"/>
    They are united in purpose and willingly hand over their power to him.
    <verse eid="REV 17:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="REV 17:14"/>
    They will wage war against the Lamb, but the Lamb will overcome them, because He is Lord of lords and King of kings—and those who belong to Him are called, chosen, and faithful.”
    <verse eid="REV 17:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="REV 17:15"/>
    Then the angel continued: “The waters you saw, where the prostitute sits, represent peoples, multitudes, nations, and languages.
    <verse eid="REV 17:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="REV 17:16"/>
    The ten horns and the beast will eventually turn against the prostitute. They will strip her, devastate her, and consume her—destroying her completely.
    <verse eid="REV 17:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="REV 17:17"/>
    For God has sovereignly moved their hearts to carry out His purpose: They will act together in giving their authority to the beast until God’s words are fulfilled.
    <verse eid="REV 17:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="REV 17:18"/>
    The woman you saw represents the great city that exercises dominion over the rulers of the earth.”
    <verse eid="REV 17:18"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="REV 17"/>
  <chapter number="18" style="c" sid="REV 18"/>
  <para style="s1">Lament Over Babylon the Great</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="REV 18:1"/>
    After these things, I saw another angel coming down from heaven, invested with great authority, and the earth was lit up by the splendor of his presence.
    <verse eid="REV 18:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="REV 18:2"/>
    He cried out loudly and forcefully:
    <verse eid="REV 18:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Babylon the great has collapsed—utterly fallen!</para>
  <para style="p">She has become a dwelling place for demons,</para>
  <para style="p">a refuge for every corrupt spirit,</para>
  <para style="p">a shelter for everything spiritually unclean and detestable.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="REV 18:3"/>
    All nations have drunk of the wine of the passion of her sexual corruption.
    <verse eid="REV 18:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">The rulers of the earth have committed sexual immorality with her,</para>
  <para style="p">and the traders of the world enriched themselves</para>
  <para style="p">by feeding on her excess and indulgence.”</para>
  <para style="s1">Warning to God’s People to Escape Babylon</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="REV 18:4"/>
    Then I heard another voice speaking from heaven:
    <verse eid="REV 18:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Come out from her, My people,</para>
  <para style="p">so that you do not share in her sins</para>
  <para style="p">and do not suffer the judgments coming upon her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="REV 18:5"/>
    Her offenses have stacked up as high as heaven itself,
    <verse eid="REV 18:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">and God has not forgotten her crimes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="REV 18:6"/>
    Give her what she gave to others;
    <verse eid="REV 18:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">pay her back in full—indeed, double—</para>
  <para style="p">pour out for her a cup twice as strong</para>
  <para style="p">as the one she prepared for others.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="REV 18:7"/>
    As much as she glorified herself and lived in self-indulgent luxury,
    <verse eid="REV 18:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">give her the same measure of agony and mourning.</para>
  <para style="p">For she boasts inwardly,</para>
  <para style="p">‘I rule as a queen.</para>
  <para style="p">I am secure, not abandoned,</para>
  <para style="p">and sorrow will never touch me.’</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="REV 18:8"/>
    Because of this arrogance, 
    <verse eid="REV 18:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">her disasters will strike suddenly in a single day—</para>
  <para style="p">death, grief, and famine—</para>
  <para style="p">and she will be burned up completely,</para>
  <para style="p">for the Lord God who judges her is mighty.”</para>
  <para style="s1">Threefold Pronouncement of God’s Judgment on Babylon</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="REV 18:9"/>
    The kings of the earth who shared her immorality and extravagance will wail when they see the smoke rising from her destruction.
    <verse eid="REV 18:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="REV 18:10"/>
    Standing far away in terror, they will cry:
    <verse eid="REV 18:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Disaster! Disaster!</para>
  <para style="p">O mighty city, Babylon the strong!</para>
  <para style="p">In a single hour your sentence has been carried out!”</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="REV 18:11"/>
    The merchants of the world will also weep and mourn over her, because no one buys their cargo anymore—
    <verse eid="REV 18:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="REV 18:12"/>
    cargo of gold, silver, precious stones, pearls; fine linen, purple, silk, scarlet; every kind of citron wood; every article of ivory; every article made from the most valuable wood, bronze, iron, or marble;
    <verse eid="REV 18:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="REV 18:13"/>
    cinnamon, spice, aromatic substances for burning, myrrh, frankincense; wine, olive oil, fine flour, wheat; cattle, sheep, horses, carriages; slaves, and human lives.
    <verse eid="REV 18:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="REV 18:14"/>
    They will lament:
    <verse eid="REV 18:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“All the things you longed for are gone.</para>
  <para style="p">Your splendor and wealth have vanished,</para>
  <para style="p">never to return.”</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="REV 18:15"/>
    Those who became rich through her will stand at a distance, shaken by fear, weeping and mourning.
    <verse eid="REV 18:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="REV 18:16"/>
    They will cry:
    <verse eid="REV 18:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Disaster! Disaster!</para>
  <para style="p">The great city clothed in luxury,</para>
  <para style="p">adorned with gold and jewels—</para>
  <para style="p">destroyed in a single hour!”</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="REV 18:17"/>
    Sailors, sea captains, traders, and all who make their living from the sea will also stand far off.
    <verse eid="REV 18:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="REV 18:18"/>
    Watching the smoke of her burning, they will ask:
    <verse eid="REV 18:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Was there ever a city like this?”</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="REV 18:19"/>
    Throwing dust on their heads, they will weep and shout:
    <verse eid="REV 18:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Disaster! Disaster!</para>
  <para style="p">The city that made us wealthy</para>
  <para style="p">through her trade—</para>
  <para style="p">brought to ruin in a single hour!”</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="REV 18:20"/>
    But rejoice over her fall, O heaven—
    <verse eid="REV 18:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">rejoice, saints, apostles, and prophets—</para>
  <para style="p">for God has finally judged her</para>
  <para style="p">for what she did to you.”</para>
  <para style="s1">The Climax of Babylon’s Destruction</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="REV 18:21"/>
    Then a powerful angel lifted a massive stone like a millstone and hurled it into the sea, declaring:
    <verse eid="REV 18:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“With this same force</para>
  <para style="p">Babylon the great city will be thrown down</para>
  <para style="p">and will never be found again.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="REV 18:22"/>
    Music and celebration will vanish from her forever.
    <verse eid="REV 18:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">No craftsman will remain,</para>
  <para style="p">no industry will survive,</para>
  <para style="p">no sound of work or life will be heard again.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="REV 18:23"/>
    No lamp will ever shine in her streets again.
    <verse eid="REV 18:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">No wedding songs will ever be heard again.</para>
  <para style="p">Her merchants once ruled the world,</para>
  <para style="p">and her sorcery deceived the nations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="REV 18:24"/>
    In her was found the blood of prophets, of God’s people, and of all who were slain across the earth.”
    <verse eid="REV 18:24"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="REV 18"/>
  <chapter number="19" style="c" sid="REV 19"/>
  <para style="s1">Heaven’s Threefold Praise</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="REV 19:1"/>
    After this, I heard what sounded like a massive crowd in heaven shouting:
    <verse eid="REV 19:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Praise the Lord!</para>
  <para style="p">Salvation, glory, and power belong to our God,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="REV 19:2"/>
    because His judgments are true and just.
    <verse eid="REV 19:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">He has condemned the corrupt system</para>
  <para style="p">that polluted the earth with immorality,</para>
  <para style="p">and He has avenged the blood of His servants.”</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="REV 19:3"/>
    Once more they shouted:
    <verse eid="REV 19:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Praise the Lord!</para>
  <para style="p">The smoke of her destruction rises forever.”</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="REV 19:4"/>
    The twenty-four elders and the four living beings fell down and worshipped God, saying:
    <verse eid="REV 19:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Amen! Praise the Lord!”</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="REV 19:5"/>
    Then a voice came from the throne:
    <verse eid="REV 19:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Praise our God, all His servants—</para>
  <para style="p">all who fear Him, great and small alike!”</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="REV 19:6"/>
    I heard what sounded like a vast multitude, like rushing waters and powerful thunder:
    <verse eid="REV 19:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Praise the Lord!</para>
  <para style="p">For the Lord God Almighty reigns!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="REV 19:7"/>
    Let us celebrate and give Him glory,
    <verse eid="REV 19:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">for the wedding of the Lamb has arrived,</para>
  <para style="p">and His bride has prepared herself.”</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="REV 19:8"/>
    She was given pure, bright linen to wear—
    <verse eid="REV 19:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">the linen symbolizing the righteous acts of God’s people.</para>
  <para style="s1">The Marriage Supper of the Lamb</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="REV 19:9"/>
    Then the angel said to me, “Write this down: Blessed are those invited to the Lamb’s wedding feast.” He added, “These are the trustworthy words of God.”
    <verse eid="REV 19:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="REV 19:10"/>
    I fell at his feet to worship him, but he said, “Stop! I am a fellow servant with you. Worship God alone. The witness of Jesus is the heart of prophecy.”
    <verse eid="REV 19:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Christ the Victorious Warrior</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="REV 19:11"/>
    Then I saw heaven opened, and there was a white horse. Its rider is called Faithful and True, and He judges and wages war in righteousness.
    <verse eid="REV 19:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="REV 19:12"/>
    His eyes burn like fire, and many crowns rest upon His head. He bears a name known only to Himself.
    <verse eid="REV 19:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="REV 19:13"/>
    He is clothed in a robe soaked in blood, and His name is called the Word of God.
    <verse eid="REV 19:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="REV 19:14"/>
    The armies of heaven follow Him, riding white horses and wearing clean, bright linen.
    <verse eid="REV 19:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="REV 19:15"/>
    A sharp sword comes from His mouth, by which He subdues the nations. He rules them with unyielding authority and executes the wrath of God Almighty.
    <verse eid="REV 19:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="REV 19:16"/>
    On His robe and on His thigh is written: 
    <verse eid="REV 19:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“King of kings and Lord of lords.”</para>
  <para style="s1">The Final Battle and Judgment</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="REV 19:17"/>
    Then I saw an angel standing in the sun, calling loudly to the birds flying in the midair: “Come, gather for the great feast of God,
    <verse eid="REV 19:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="REV 19:18"/>
    to consume the flesh of the kings, generals, mighty warriors, and all people, whether free or enslaved.”
    <verse eid="REV 19:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="REV 19:19"/>
    I saw the beast, the rulers of the earth, and their armies assembled to wage war against the rider on the horse and His army.
    <verse eid="REV 19:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="REV 19:20"/>
    The beast was captured, along with the false prophet who had carried out miraculous signs in the beast’s presence—signs through which he deceived those who had accepted the beast’s mark and given allegiance to its image. Both were thrown alive into the lake of fire, a place of burning sulfur. 
    <verse eid="REV 19:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="REV 19:21"/>
    The remaining forces were destroyed by the sword from Christ’s mouth, and the birds were filled with their flesh.
    <verse eid="REV 19:21"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="REV 19"/>
  <chapter number="20" style="c" sid="REV 20"/>
  <para style="s1">The Binding of Satan</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="REV 20:1"/>
    I saw an angel descending from heaven, holding authority over the abyss and carrying a heavy chain.
    <verse eid="REV 20:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="REV 20:2"/>
    He overpowered the dragon—the ancient serpent known as the devil and Satan—and bound him for a thousand years.
    <verse eid="REV 20:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="REV 20:3"/>
    He confined him to the abyss, shutting and sealing it, so that he could no longer deceive the nations during this appointed period. Afterward, he must be released briefly, according to God’s purpose.
    <verse eid="REV 20:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Millennial Reign of Christ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="REV 20:4"/>
    I then saw thrones, and those seated on them were granted authority to judge. I also saw the souls of those who had been beheaded because of their witness to Jesus and their loyalty to God’s word. They had refused allegiance to the beast and its image and had not accepted its mark. They were raised to life and reigned together with Christ for a thousand years.
    <verse eid="REV 20:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="REV 20:5"/>
    The rest of the dead were not raised until this period had ended. This is the first resurrection.
    <verse eid="REV 20:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="REV 20:6"/>
    Those who share in it are blessed and set apart for God. The second death has no claim over them. They serve God and Christ as priests and reign with Him throughout this thousand-year reign.
    <verse eid="REV 20:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Final Defeat of Satan</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="REV 20:7"/>
    When the thousand years are completed, Satan will be released from his confinement.
    <verse eid="REV 20:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="REV 20:8"/>
    He will again mislead the nations across the whole earth—symbolized by Gog and Magog—assembling them for rebellion. Their number will be vast beyond counting.
    <verse eid="REV 20:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="REV 20:9"/>
    They will advance across the land and surround God’s people and the city He loves. But fire will descend from heaven and destroy them.
    <verse eid="REV 20:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="REV 20:10"/>
    The devil, who deceived them, will be cast into the lake of fire and sulfur, where the beast and the false prophet already are, and they will face unending judgment.
    <verse eid="REV 20:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Great White Throne Judgment</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="REV 20:11"/>
    Then I saw a great white throne and the One seated upon it. The earth and the sky fled from His presence, leaving no place to hide.
    <verse eid="REV 20:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="REV 20:12"/>
    All the dead, from the least to the greatest, were standing before the throne. Books were opened, and another book was opened—the book of life. Each person was judged on the basis of their deeds, as they were written in the books.
    <verse eid="REV 20:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="REV 20:13"/>
    The sea gave up its dead, and Death and Hades released those under their power. All were judged individually according to what they had done.
    <verse eid="REV 20:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="REV 20:14"/>
    Death and Hades themselves were thrown into the lake of fire. This is the second death.
    <verse eid="REV 20:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="REV 20:15"/>
    Anyone whose name was not found written in the book of life was also thrown into the lake of fire.
    <verse eid="REV 20:15"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="REV 20"/>
  <chapter number="21" style="c" sid="REV 21"/>
  <para style="s1">The New Heaven and the New Earth</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="REV 21:1"/>
    I saw a new heaven and a new earth, for the former creation had passed away, and the sea was no more.
    <verse eid="REV 21:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="REV 21:2"/>
    I saw the holy city, the new Jerusalem, descending from God out of heaven, prepared like a bride beautifully dressed for her husband.
    <verse eid="REV 21:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="REV 21:3"/>
    Then I heard a powerful voice coming from the throne announcing, “Look—the dwelling place of God is with men. He will live with them, and they will belong to Him. God Himself will be present with them as their God.
    <verse eid="REV 21:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="REV 21:4"/>
    He will remove every tear from their eyes, and death will no longer exist. There will be no mourning, no crying, and no pain anymore, because the former world and its suffering have come to an end.”
    <verse eid="REV 21:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="REV 21:5"/>
    The One seated on the throne said, “I am making all things new.” Then He said, “Write this down, for these words are faithful and true.”
    <verse eid="REV 21:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="REV 21:6"/>
    He said to me, “It is finished. I am the Alpha and the Omega, the beginning and the end—the origin and the goal of all things. To anyone who thirsts, I will freely give water from the spring of life.
    <verse eid="REV 21:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="REV 21:7"/>
    Those who overcome will inherit these blessings. I will be their God, and they will be My children.
    <verse eid="REV 21:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="REV 21:8"/>
    But the fearful, unbelieving, morally corrupt, murderers, sexually immoral, sorcerers, idolaters, and all liars will be sentenced to the lake of fire, which is the second death.”
    <verse eid="REV 21:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The New Jerusalem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="REV 21:9"/>
    One of the angels who carried the final plagues said to me, “Come, I will show you the bride, the Lamb’s wife.”
    <verse eid="REV 21:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="REV 21:10"/>
    Carried by the Spirit to a great and high mountain, he showed me the holy city, Jerusalem, descending from God in heaven.
    <verse eid="REV 21:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="REV 21:11"/>
    It reflects God’s glory, shining like a precious jewel, like a jasper, clear and radiant.
    <verse eid="REV 21:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="REV 21:12"/>
    The city has a great and high wall with twelve gates, guarded by angels, and inscribed with the names of Israel’s twelve tribes.
    <verse eid="REV 21:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="REV 21:13"/>
    There are three gates on each side of the city—east, north, south, and west.
    <verse eid="REV 21:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="REV 21:14"/>
    The city wall has twelve foundations bearing the names of the twelve apostles of the Lamb.
    <verse eid="REV 21:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="REV 21:15"/>
    The angel measured the city and its gates and walls with a golden measuring rod.
    <verse eid="REV 21:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="REV 21:16"/>
    The city is designed with perfect symmetry, forming a square, with its length and width identical. When the angel measured it with the measuring rod, it extended 12, 000 stadia in every direction—its length, width, and height all being the same. 
    <verse eid="REV 21:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="REV 21:17"/>
    He also measured its wall, which was 144 cubits thick, using the standard human measurement that the angel likewise employed.
    <verse eid="REV 21:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="REV 21:18"/>
    The wall is built of jasper, and the city itself is made of pure gold, clear like glass.
    <verse eid="REV 21:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="REV 21:19"/>
    The foundations of the city’s wall are adorned with every variety of precious stone. The first foundation is jasper, the second sapphire, the third chalcedony, the fourth emerald, 
    <verse eid="REV 21:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="REV 21:20"/>
    the fifth sardonyx, the sixth sardius, the seventh chrysolite, the eighth beryl, the ninth topaz, the tenth chrysoprase, the eleventh jacinth, the twelfth amethyst. 
    <verse eid="REV 21:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="REV 21:21"/>
    The twelve gates are twelve pearls, each one of the gates was made from a single pearl. And the street of the city is pure gold, like transparent glass. 
    <verse eid="REV 21:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="REV 21:22"/>
    I saw no temple there, because the Lord God Almighty and the Lamb themselves are its temple.
    <verse eid="REV 21:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="REV 21:23"/>
    The city needs no sun or moon, for God’s glory illuminates it, and the Lamb is its light.
    <verse eid="REV 21:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="REV 21:24"/>
    The nations walk by that light, and earthly rulers bring their honor into it.
    <verse eid="REV 21:24"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="REV 21:25"/>
    Its gates are never shut, because there is no night.
    <verse eid="REV 21:25"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="REV 21:26"/>
    The glory and honor of the nations are brought into it.
    <verse eid="REV 21:26"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="REV 21:27"/>
    Nothing impure will enter—only those whose names are written in the Lamb’s book of life.
    <verse eid="REV 21:27"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="REV 21"/>
  <chapter number="22" style="c" sid="REV 22"/>
  <para style="s1">The River of Life</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="REV 22:1"/>
    The angel showed me the river of life, bright as crystal, flowing from the throne of God and the Lamb.
    <verse eid="REV 22:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="REV 22:2"/>
    It runs through the center of the city. On both sides stand the tree of life, producing twelve kinds of fruit, yielding its fruit every month. Its leaves bring healing to the nations.
    <verse eid="REV 22:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="REV 22:3"/>
    There will no longer be any curse, and the throne of God and of the Lamb will be in it, and His servants will serve Him.
    <verse eid="REV 22:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="REV 22:4"/>
    They will see His face, and His name will be written on their foreheads, marking them as His own.
    <verse eid="REV 22:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="REV 22:5"/>
    There will be no night. They will need no lamp or sunlight, because God Himself will give them light, and they will reign forever.
    <verse eid="REV 22:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">John and the Angel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="REV 22:6"/>
    The angel said, “These words are reliable and true. The Lord, the God who inspires and speaks through the prophets, sent His angel to show His servants what must soon take place.”
    <verse eid="REV 22:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="REV 22:7"/>
    “Look, I am coming soon. Blessed is the one who keeps the words of the prophecy of this book.”
    <verse eid="REV 22:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="REV 22:8"/>
    I, John, heard and saw these things. Overwhelmed, I fell down to worship the angel who had been showing them to me.
    <verse eid="REV 22:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="REV 22:9"/>
    He said to me, “Do not do that. I am a fellow servant with you and with your fellow prophets and with all who keep the words of this book. Direct your worship to God alone.”
    <verse eid="REV 22:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="REV 22:10"/>
    Then he told me, “Do not keep the words of this prophecy hidden, because the time for their fulfillment is near.
    <verse eid="REV 22:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="REV 22:11"/>
    Let those who persist in wrongdoing continue in it; let those who remain morally defiled remain so. Likewise, let those who are righteous continue to live rightly, and let those who are holy continue in holiness.”
    <verse eid="REV 22:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="REV 22:12"/>
    “Pay attention—I am coming soon, and I bring with Me what each person is due, repaying everyone according to what they have done.
    <verse eid="REV 22:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="REV 22:13"/>
    I am the Alpha and the Omega, the beginning and the end—the first and the last, the origin and the goal of all things.”
    <verse eid="REV 22:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="REV 22:14"/>
    Blessed are those who have been cleansed, for they are granted access to the tree of life and are allowed to enter the city through its gates.
    <verse eid="REV 22:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="REV 22:15"/>
    Outside remain the dogs and those who practice occult arts, sexual immorality, murder, idolatry, and everyone who loves and lives by falsehood.
    <verse eid="REV 22:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="REV 22:16"/>
    “I, Jesus, have sent My angel to testify to you about these matters for the sake of the churches. I  am the Root and the Offspring of David, the radiant Morning Star.”
    <verse eid="REV 22:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="REV 22:17"/>
    The Spirit and the bride extend the invitation, saying, “Come.” Let anyone who hears respond to that call. Let the one who is thirsty come forward; whoever desires may freely receive the water that gives life.
    <verse eid="REV 22:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="REV 22:18"/>
    I solemnly warn everyone who hears the words of this prophetic book: If anyone adds to them, God will add to that person the judgments described here.
    <verse eid="REV 22:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="REV 22:19"/>
    And if anyone removes anything from the words of this prophecy, God will remove that person’s share in the tree of life and in the holy city described in this book.
    <verse eid="REV 22:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="REV 22:20"/>
    The One who testifies to these things declares, “Yes, I am coming soon.” Amen. Come, Lord Jesus.
    <verse eid="REV 22:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="REV 22:21"/>
    May the grace of the Lord Jesus be with all God’s people. Amen.
    <verse eid="REV 22:21"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="REV 22"/>
</usx>
